    title: "歐盟《網路韌性法案》（CRA）正式生效，要求數位產品製造商必須納入強制性資安義務",
    summary: "歐盟正式實施《網路韌性法案》（Cyber Resilience Act, CRA），這是首個對包含數位元素的產品強制規定資安要求的歐盟法規。該法案大幅提升了製造商的責任，要求他們必須確保硬體與軟體產品的安全性。核心義務包括提供修補安全漏洞的軟體更新，並為消費者提供持續的資安支援。產品若符合規定，將需貼上 CE 標記。根據歐盟委員會執行副主席 Henna Virkkunen 的說明，此法案旨在降低歐盟市場數位產品帶來的網路風險。該法案與已生效的 NIS2 資安框架互補，是歐盟強化數位安全體系的重大舉措。主要的法規義務將從 2027 年 12 月 11 日開始適用。",
    tags: ["Cyber Resilience Act", "CRA", "歐盟", "資安法規", "CE 標記", "NIS2"],
    title_en: "EU's Cyber Resilience Act (CRA) Officially Takes Effect, Mandating Cybersecurity Obligations for Digital Product Manufacturers",
    summary_en: "The EU has officially implemented the Cyber Resilience Act (CRA), which is the first EU regulation to mandate cybersecurity requirements for products containing digital elements. This law significantly increases manufacturer responsibility, requiring them to ensure the security of both hardware and software products. Core obligations include providing software updates to patch security vulnerabilities and offering continuous cybersecurity support to consumers. Products that comply with the regulations will need to bear the CE mark. According to EU Commission Vice-President Henna Virkkunen, the Act aims to reduce the cyber risk posed by digital products in the EU market. The Act complements the already effective NIS2 cybersecurity framework and represents a major step by the EU in strengthening its digital security system. The primary regulatory obligations will become applicable starting December 11, 2027.",
